{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773086822,"nonce":"haNCPY3yHYnmlZFIjKXFE1LM6rQ=","title":"graph API: post-collection limit creates type bias + repo filter uses path.basename","message":"Two design issues in GET /api/graph:\n\n1. Type bias from post-collection limit: nodes from all types are merged, sorted by created_at desc, then capped at limit. With many recent sessions (40) and fewer issues (10), branch nodes get evicted even when connected. Fix: apply per-type caps (limit/4 each) or use a connectivity-aware relevance sort.\n\n2. Repo filter uses path.basename(cwd): Sessions are filtered by path.basename(s.cwd), which is wrong for worktree sessions whose cwd is .../repo/worktrees/feature__foo. The work-scanner registry already maps repo_root → repo_name; use it instead. Same issue for branch nodes.\n\nThese affect graph completeness when filtering by repo, especially with worktree-based sessions.\n\nBug: fe566dc","files":null}]}